DICTIONARY CLAIMS UNDER TEST:
 (C1) nonloc == 0 for all shapes  => T(x) is a.e. a ROUND tournament  [HYP-2576].
 (C2) measN (1/7-net) = P[no empty 1/7-arc] = P[T(x) strongly-connected-ish + dense].
 (C3) mu_1/7 = P[maxgap>1/7] = P[ some vertex's clockwise gap to its successor >1/7 ].
      In round-tournament terms: the consecutive-on-circle pair (v, succ(v)) with the
      empty arc is a 'NEAR-DOMINANCE' edge.  mu_1/7 = P[ >=1 such weak edge ].
 (C4) AP {0..k-1}: does it EXTREMISE E[c3] / E[maxscore] / measN among shapes?
